  issn = {1000-8020 (Print) 1000-8020},
  abstract = {Literature shows that not only high-concentration environmental lead exposure can cause adverse influence on the neural systems of fetuses/infants, even the low levels of environmental lead exposure can cause dysplasia in the aspects of cognition, memory, feeling and etc. Meanwhile, the psychological stimulation acception during pregnancy may also cause adverse impact on neuro-developmental of fetuses and infants. This article will make a brief review on the combined functions and relative mechanisms, when a pregnant woman experiences psychological stimulation acception and lead exposure.},
